            <div xml:id="d384">

                <pb facs="0573" n="459" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg459"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">814.00/653: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Curtis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-02-22T16:00:00-07:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 22,
                                1922—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received February 23—1:35
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>17. Election finished. Legation latest returns are over 168,000 for General
                    Orellana the only official candidate, and about 400 scattering.</p>
                <p>In addition to the disturbances reported in my telegram February 7 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">17</hi>], 5 p.m.,<anchor n="3" xml:id="d384-f1"/> there
                    was an uprising at Escuintla on Saturday night with at least 7 killed.
                    Apparently there has [<hi rendition="#italic">have</hi>] been no other disorders
                    of this sort.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Curtis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
